# btc-quant collector — environment for the systemd services.
#
#   cp env.example env  &&  chmod 600 env   (then fill HF_TOKEN)
#
# The real `env` file is gitignored and never committed. bootstrap.sh installs it
# to @APP_DIR@/deploy/gcp/env, owned by the service user, mode 600.

# Hugging Face WRITE token, scoped to the dataset only. Create at
# https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens -> "Fine-grained" -> write access to
# azulcoder/btc-quant-ticks (nothing else). huggingface_hub reads HF_TOKEN
# automatically (scripts/upload_hf.py never prints it). A dataset-scoped token
# means a leak cannot touch the rest of the account.
HF_TOKEN=

# Symbol the collector records. The rotation store is per-symbol (DESIGN §3c); a
# different symbol here is a different store — the same honest-restart rule as the
# terminal. Recording scope this phase matches the Mac launchd unit: one symbol,
# bybit-linear as the primary full-book leg plus the supplementary cross-venue trade
# and depth streams the collector pulls keyless by default (binancef, OKX, Coinbase,
# Deribit). Adding full-depth books / spot legs is a separate, disk/cost-gated decision
# documented in README.md "Phase 2".
BTCQUANT_SYMBOL=BTCUSDT
